(380, 1, '1', '5', 'AI &amp; SEO', '2025-08-07', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\">Ms. Nayanaba Gohil, a distinguished professional in the field of digital marketing and search engine optimization (SEO), is currently associated with Mitanshi Technologies, a leading IT company based in Bhavnagar, Gujarat. With a strong academic background and a passion for technology, Ms. Gohil has established herself as a thought leader in the integration of Artificial Intelligence (AI) with SEO strategies.</p>\r\n', '2025-09-10-64-7-8-25_Expert Talk_3rd_B.Tech_X.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-09-10 11:28:55', '2025-09-10 11:28:55', NULL, NULL),
(381, 1, '1', '562', 'AI &amp; SEO', '2025-08-07', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\">Ms. Nayanaba Gohil, a distinguished professional in the field of digital marketing and search engine optimization (SEO), is currently associated with Mitanshi Technologies, a leading IT company based in Bhavnagar, Gujarat. With a strong academic background and a passion for technology, Ms. Gohil has established herself as a thought leader in the integration of Artificial Intelligence (AI) with SEO strategies.</p>\r\n', '2025-09-10-61-7-8-25_Expert Talk_Premium_1st_B.Tech._CSE1.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-09-10 11:45:31', '2025-09-10 11:45:31', NULL, NULL),
(382, 1, '5', '564', 'Expert talk on Memory Magic: Arrays &amp; Pointers', '2025-09-13', '<p>The online expert talk, <em>&ldquo;Memory Magic: Arrays &amp; Pointers&rdquo;</em>, was organized for Diploma IT 1st semester students under the Premium Program. Conducted by Ms. Disha Shukla from Nova Techset, the session ran from 11:00 AM to 1:00 PM on 13th September 2025. The talk aimed at simplifying the often challenging concepts of arrays and pointers in C programming by explaining them step by step with relatable examples. Ms. Shukla connected theoretical knowledge with practical applications, demonstrating how these fundamentals are applied in real-world IT solutions. The session was interactive, student-friendly, and highly impactful, leaving participants motivated to strengthen their basics and explore programming with greater confidence.</p>\r\n', '2025-09-15-19-Premium Program expert talk Diploma (1st) 13-09.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-09-15 10:24:15', '2025-09-15 10:24:15', NULL, NULL),
(383, 1, '5', '23', 'Expert Talk on Cloud Computing and Its Importance in the Digital Era', '2025-09-19', '<p>The Department of Information Technology, Gyanmanjari Innovative University, organized an Expert Talk on <strong>19th September 2025</strong> for Diploma IT 5th Semester students (Classes D, E, F &amp; G). The session was delivered by <strong>Mr. Shubham Shah</strong> from <strong>Millople Technologies, Bhavnagar</strong>, who shared valuable insights into the fundamentals and real-world applications of <strong>Cloud Computing</strong>. Students learned about cloud infrastructure, scalability, flexibility, and its role in transforming modern businesses. The talk also highlighted career opportunities and future trends in cloud technology, bridging the gap between classroom concepts and industry practices. The session proved to be highly engaging and motivating, inspiring students to explore cloud computing as a vital skill for their professional growth.</p>\r\n', '2025-09-25-44-expert talk Diploma (5th) 19-09.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-09-25 10:16:10', '2025-09-25 10:16:10', NULL, NULL),
(384, 1, '5', '23', 'Alumni Interaction', '2025-09-22', '<p>The Alumni Interaction Session held on 22nd September 2025 at GyanManjari Innovative University featured Shri Pranjal Upadhyay, a distinguished alumnus of the IT Department and Cybersecurity Expert at Rashtriya Raksha University, who shared his professional journey and expertise in areas such as background verification, digital footprint analysis, and network security; through practical demonstrations on website blocking, traffic redirection, and network control, he connected academic concepts with real-world applications, while also guiding students on placement readiness, career opportunities, and industry-relevant skills, making the session highly insightful, interactive, and motivational for Diploma IT 5th semester students.</p>\r\n', '2025-09-30-42-Alumni Interaction Diploma (5th) 22-09.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-09-30 04:56:44', '2025-09-30 04:56:44', NULL, NULL),
(385, 1, '1', '6', 'Professional Career Guidance Session on GATE Awareness', '2025-10-06', '<p>The Department of Information Technology, Gyanmanjari Innovative University, organized a <em>Professional Career Guidance Session</em> on <strong>GATE Awareness</strong> for B.Tech 5th Semester students on <strong>6th October 2025</strong>. The expert talk was delivered by <strong>Ms. Keertana Nair</strong> from <strong>IIT Bombay</strong>, who shared valuable insights into GATE&rsquo;s structure, preparation strategies, and its role in shaping technical careers. The session aimed to motivate students to view GATE not merely as an exam but as a transformative journey toward analytical excellence and higher education opportunities. Interactive discussions and practical guidance inspired students to pursue focused preparation with confidence.</p>\r\n', '2025-10-09-57-Professional Career Guidance B.Tech (5th-C) 06-10.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-10-09 04:31:52', '2025-10-09 04:31:52', NULL, NULL),
(386, 1, '1', '3', 'An Expert Talk on Machine Learning and AI', '2025-07-18', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><u><em><strong>Objective</strong></em></u><br />\r\nAn expert talk for engineering students should aim to bridge the gap between academic knowledge<br />\r\nand real-world applications, offering students valuable insights into current industry trends and<br />\r\ninnovations. By highlighting the practical applications of theoretical concepts, the speaker can<br />\r\ndemonstrate how the knowledge gained in the classroom translates to impactful solutions in the field.<br />\r\nSuch talks also play a crucial role in guiding students on career pathways and skill development,<br />\r\nhelping them understand the essential technical and soft skills that are valued in today&rsquo;s job market.<br />\r\nBeyond technical knowledge, expert talks encourage interdisciplinary awareness, fostering an<br />\r\nunderstanding of how collaboration across fields can solve complex engineering challenges.<br />\r\nAdditionally, students gain exposure to the importance of sustainable practices and ethical<br />\r\nresponsibilities, reinforcing the role of engineers in addressing environmental and societal issues. By<br />\r\ninspiring students to think critically, innovate, and embrace lifelong learning, expert talks prepare<br />\r\nthem to adapt and thrive in the ever-evolving engineering landscape.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><em><strong><u>About Activities:</u></strong></em><br />\r\nAn expert talk on &ldquo;PLC SCADA &rdquo; was successfully organized on 18th July 2025 (Friday) at Room<br />\r\nNo. TF-14, specifically for the students of EC and Computer Engineering branches (Diploma &amp;<br />\r\nDegree).<br />\r\nThe seminar was conducted by Sofcon India Pvt. Ltd., a National Skill Development Corporation<br />\r\n(NSDC) and Ministry of Skill Development &amp; Entrepreneurship (MSDE) affiliated company, also</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\">associated with ESSCI, IASC, and HSSC. The primary objective of the event was to provide industry-<br />\r\noriented knowledge and practical exposure related to the rapidly evolving field of Artificial</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\">Intelligence and Machine Learning (AI-ML).<br />\r\nThe keynote speakers were:<br />\r\n● Mr. Vishal Vadher, Training Manager<br />\r\n● Mr. Harvish Upadhyay, Automation Engineer<br />\r\nThe experts shared valuable insights on how automation and digital technologies are shaping modern<br />\r\nindustries. Key topics included real-time control systems, industrial communication, AI-ML<br />\r\napplications, and trends in smart manufacturing. The session also highlighted career opportunities</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\">and essential skills for future engineers. An interactive Q&amp;A allowed students to clarify doubts. E-<br />\r\ncertificates were issued to registered participants. The seminar was well-received, enriching students</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\">with practical knowledge and motivating them to explore careers in emerging technologies.</p>\r\n', '2025-10-19-97-3. Expert Talk_BE3_EC.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-10-19 16:10:03', '2025-10-19 16:10:03', NULL, NULL),
(387, 1, '1', '212', 'An Expert Talk on Machine Learning and AI', '2025-07-18', '<p><em><u><strong>Objective</strong></u></em><br />\r\nAn expert talk for engineering students should aim to bridge the gap between academic knowledge<br />\r\nand real-world applications, offering students valuable insights into current industry trends and<br />\r\ninnovations. By highlighting the practical applications of theoretical concepts, the speaker can<br />\r\ndemonstrate how the knowledge gained in the classroom translates to impactful solutions in the field.<br />\r\nSuch talks also play a crucial role in guiding students on career pathways and skill development,<br />\r\nhelping them understand the essential technical and soft skills that are valued in today&rsquo;s job market.<br />\r\nBeyond technical knowledge, expert talks encourage interdisciplinary awareness, fostering an<br />\r\nunderstanding of how collaboration across fields can solve complex engineering challenges.<br />\r\nAdditionally, students gain exposure to the importance of sustainable practices and ethical<br />\r\nresponsibilities, reinforcing the role of engineers in addressing environmental and societal issues. By<br />\r\ninspiring students to think critically, innovate, and embrace lifelong learning, expert talks prepare<br />\r\nthem to adapt and thrive in the ever-evolving engineering landscape.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><u><em><strong>About Activities:</strong></em></u><br />\r\nAn expert talk on &ldquo;PLC SCADA &rdquo; was successfully organized on 18th July 2025 (Friday) at Room<br />\r\nNo. TF-14, specifically for the students of EC and Computer Engineering branches (Diploma &amp;<br />\r\nDegree).<br />\r\nThe seminar was conducted by Sofcon India Pvt. Ltd., a National Skill Development Corporation<br />\r\n(NSDC) and Ministry of Skill Development &amp; Entrepreneurship (MSDE) affiliated company, also</p>\r\n\r\n<p>associated with ESSCI, IASC, and HSSC. The primary objective of the event was to provide industry-<br />\r\noriented knowledge and practical exposure related to the rapidly evolving field of Artificial</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Intelligence and Machine Learning (AI-ML).<br />\r\nThe keynote speakers were:<br />\r\n● Mr. Vishal Vadher, Training Manager<br />\r\n● Mr. Harvish Upadhyay, Automation Engineer<br />\r\nThe experts shared valuable insights on how automation and digital technologies are shaping modern<br />\r\nindustries. Key topics included real-time control systems, industrial communication, AI-ML<br />\r\napplications, and trends in smart manufacturing. The session also highlighted career opportunities</p>\r\n\r\n<p>and essential skills for future engineers. An interactive Q&amp;A allowed students to clarify doubts. E-<br />\r\ncertificates were issued to registered participants. The seminar was well-received, enriching students</p>\r\n\r\n<p>with practical knowledge and motivating them to explore careers in emerging technologies.</p>\r\n', '2025-10-19-65-3. Expert Talk_BE3_EC.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-10-19 16:35:39', '2025-10-19 16:35:39', NULL, NULL),
(388, 1, '1', '212', 'Expert Talk By Tricks Robotics', '2025-02-12', '<p><span style=\"font-size:16pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Times New Roman\',serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><strong>About Workshop:</strong></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Times New Roman\',serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">A workshop on &quot;Expert Talk By tricks robotics&quot; was held on [12/02/2025] at [XF-01], bringing together professionals, academics, and students to discuss the latest advancements and innovations in the field of electrical engineering. The event aimed to provide a platform for knowledge exchange, networking, and collaboration among participants.</span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Times New Roman\',serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><strong>Objective&nbsp;</strong></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Times New Roman\',serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The primary objectives of the workshop were:</span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n	<li style=\"list-style-type:decimal\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Times New Roman\',serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">To introduce participants to emerging technologies and trends in electrical engineering.</span></span></span></li>\r\n	<li style=\"list-style-type:decimal\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Times New Roman\',serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">To provide insights into practical applications of modern electrical engineering concepts.</span></span></span></li>\r\n	<li style=\"list-style-type:decimal\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Times New Roman\',serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">To encourage interaction and discussion among industry experts, academics, and students.</span></span></span></li>\r\n	<li style=\"list-style-type:decimal\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Times New Roman\',serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">To explore the challenges and opportunities in adopting new technologies</span></span></span></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<p><br />\r\n&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size:16pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Times New Roman\',serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><strong>About Workshop Session</strong></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Times New Roman\',serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The workshop successfully achieved its objectives, providing attendees with a comprehensive overview of trends in electrical engineering trick robotics. The event fostered collaboration and knowledge sharing, equipping participants with the tools and insights needed to navigate the rapidly evolving landscape of electrical engineering.</span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n', '2025-10-19-15-2025-02-21-66-EXPERT TALK DEGREE UPDATED.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-10-19 16:47:13', '2025-10-19 16:47:13', NULL, NULL),
(389, 1, '5', '24', 'An Expert Talk on PLC-SCADA', '2025-07-18', '<p><u><em><strong>Objective</strong></em></u><br />\r\nAn expert talk for engineering students should aim to bridge the gap between academic knowledge<br />\r\nand real-world applications, offering students valuable insights into current industry trends and<br />\r\ninnovations. By highlighting the practical applications of theoretical concepts, the speaker can<br />\r\ndemonstrate how the knowledge gained in the classroom translates to impactful solutions in the field.<br />\r\nSuch talks also play a crucial role in guiding students on career pathways and skill development,<br />\r\nhelping them understand the essential technical and soft skills that are valued in today&rsquo;s job market.<br />\r\nBeyond technical knowledge, expert talks encourage interdisciplinary awareness, fostering an<br />\r\nunderstanding of how collaboration across fields can solve complex engineering challenges.<br />\r\nAdditionally, students gain exposure to the importance of sustainable practices and ethical<br />\r\nresponsibilities, reinforcing the role of engineers in addressing environmental and societal issues. By<br />\r\ninspiring students to think critically, innovate, and embrace lifelong learning, expert talks prepare<br />\r\nthem to adapt and thrive in the ever-evolving engineering landscape.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><u><em><strong>About Activities:</strong></em></u><br />\r\nAn expert talk on &ldquo;PLC SCADA &rdquo; was successfully organized on 18th July 2025 (Friday) at Room<br />\r\nNo. GF-28, specifically for the students of Mechanical, Aeronautical, Electrical, Civil branches<br />\r\n(Diploma &amp; Degree).<br />\r\nThe seminar was conducted by Sofcon India Pvt. Ltd., a National Skill Development Corporation<br />\r\n(NSDC) and Ministry of Skill Development &amp; Entrepreneurship (MSDE) affiliated company, also</p>\r\n\r\n<p>associated with ESSCI, IASC, and HSSC. The primary objective of the event was to provide industry-<br />\r\noriented knowledge and practical exposure related to Industrial Automation, PLC SCADA systems,</p>\r\n\r\n<p>and the rapidly evolving field of Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning (AI-ML).<br />\r\nThe keynote speakers were:<br />\r\n● Mr. Vishal Vadher, Training Manager<br />\r\n● Mr. Harvish Upadhyay, Automation Engineer<br />\r\nThe experts shared valuable insights on how automation and digital technologies are shaping modern<br />\r\nindustries. Key topics included real-time control systems, industrial communication, AI-ML<br />\r\napplications, and trends in smart manufacturing. The session also highlighted career opportunities</p>\r\n\r\n<p>and essential skills for future engineers. An interactive Q&amp;A allowed students to clarify doubts. E-<br />\r\ncertificates were issued to registered participants. The seminar was well-received, enriching students</p>\r\n\r\n<p>with practical knowledge and motivating them to explore careers in emerging technologies.</p>\r\n', '2025-10-19-64-Expert Talk_Diploma_(EE)_(3th & 5th)_(18-07- 2025).pdf', 1, 0, '2025-10-19 17:20:50', '2025-10-19 17:20:50', NULL, NULL),
