(306, 1, '1', '5', '2025-03-05', '2025', 'BISAG-N GANDHINAGAR', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\">BISAG-N provides specialized services and solutions in implementing map-based Geographic Information Systems. BISAG-N undertakes all services for the entire process of implementing an enterprise level GIS system. These services include GIS database design and development, map creation/updation and finishing, data migration/conversion and format translation, software development and customization, systems integration and technical consulting. BISAG-N also provides complete GIS solutions, which bundle hardware and software with GIS systems development services.</p>\r\n', '2025-03-28-50-Industrial Visit_BISAG-N_4BD_4-3-2025 .pdf', 1, 0, '2025-03-28 09:22:00', '2025-03-28 09:22:00', NULL, NULL),
(307, 1, '1', '6', '2025-04-20', '2025', 'Odoo India Pvt Ltd.', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,serif\"><strong>Odoo, </strong>a Belgian-origin company, offers a comprehensive suite of open-source business applications designed to meet various organizational needs, including CRM, e-Commerce, accounting, inventory, point of sale, and project management. Globally, Odoo has established a significant presence, with over 2,800 employees, 5,000 partners, and serving more than 12 million users<span style=\"font-size:10.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,sans-serif\">.</span></span></span></span></p>\r\n', '2025-04-09-17-Degree-6th_Industry Visit.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-04-09 09:27:50', '2025-04-09 09:27:50', NULL, NULL),
(308, 1, '5', '25', '2025-03-06', '2025', 'BISAG-N', '<p>BISAG-N offers comprehensive services for implementing enterprise-level Geographic Information Systems (GIS), including GIS database design, map creation and updating, data migration, software development, system integration, and technical consulting. It delivers end-to-end GIS solutions by combining hardware, software, and development services to meet diverse geospatial needs.</p>\r\n', '2025-04-15-88-Industrial_Visit_BISAG_N_4ABC_6_3_2025__1742801314.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-04-15 08:29:38', '2025-04-15 08:29:38', NULL, NULL),
(309, 1, '1', '9', '2025-02-21', '2025', 'Industrial Visit', '<p><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Times New Roman\',serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The visit aimed to enhance understanding of sustainable agricultural practices, microbial and biochemical processes involved in organic fertilizer production, and quality control measures. It also provided exposure to industrial-scale biofertilizer production, waste management strategies, and the role of biotechnology in improving soil health and crop productivity.</span></span></span></p>\r\n', '2025-05-06-67-INDUSTRIAL VISIT.docx.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-05-06 11:23:56', '2025-05-06 11:23:56', NULL, NULL),
(310, 1, '5', '23', '2025-06-20', '2025', 'Western Railway Workshop ', '<p>Western Railway &ndash; Bhavnagar Division is a vital part of the Indian Railways<br />\r\nnetwork, playing a significant role in regional connectivity, infrastructure<br />\r\ndevelopment, and public transport management. The division manages both<br />\r\npassenger and freight services, ensuring smooth operations across multiple<br />\r\nstations and routes. It oversees maintenance and operations of trains, track<br />\r\nsystems, and station facilities, contributing to economic growth and social<br />\r\nmobility in Gujarat and surrounding regions. Western Railway also supports<br />\r\nnational logistics through freight transport, parcel services, and industrial<br />\r\nlinkages.</p>\r\n', '2025-06-25-56-Railway - 20062025.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-06-25 17:00:56', '2025-06-25 17:00:56', NULL, NULL),
(311, 1, '5', '23', '2025-06-26', '2025', 'Village Visit at Bandariya', '<p>Kendravati School, located in Bandariya village, serves as a primary educational institution<br />\r\ncatering to children from the surrounding rural community. The school operates under the state<br />\r\neducation board and provides classes from Grade 1 to Grade 8. With a total enrollment of<br />\r\napproximately [insert number if known, e.g., &ldquo;120 students&rdquo;], Kendravati School is an important<br />\r\ncenter for foundational learning in the region.</p>\r\n', '2025-06-28-80-26_06_2025 Village visit.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-06-28 12:16:59', '2025-06-28 12:16:59', NULL, NULL),
(312, 1, '1', '6', '2025-07-01', '2025', 'Village Visit at Nari ', '<p>On 01/07/2025, Prof. Japan M. Mavani and Prof. Trupti H. Dharkar set out from the<br />\r\nGMIU campus to visit Shree Jagdishshwaranand Primary School in Nari village with<br />\r\nthe primary aim of observing firsthand how a rural institution can leverage<br />\r\ncommunity support and practical learning to enhance both academic and life-skill<br />\r\ndevelopment. We wished to understand the everyday realities faced by students and<br />\r\nteachers, to see how subject-specific classrooms and a well-stocked library are<br />\r\nutilized, and to evaluate the impact of initiatives such as the midday-meal scheme,<br />\r\nperiodic health camps, and the villagers&rsquo; generous ?40 lakh donation drive.</p>\r\n', '2025-07-01-57-01_07_2025 B.Tech Class Y Village visit.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-07-01 15:40:19', '2025-07-01 15:40:19', NULL, NULL),
(313, 1, '5', '23', '2025-07-07', '2025', 'Victoria Park Visit', '<p>The educational visit to Victoria Park, Bhavnagar, was organized to provide Diploma Semester 1 students with a practical understanding of ecological and environmental concepts. Surrounded by the park&rsquo;s rich biodiversity, students explored topics like conservation, ecology, and biodiversity in a real-world setting. Observing plant and animal life firsthand deepened their appreciation for ecological balance and the significance of urban green spaces. The experience also encouraged environmental awareness and personal responsibility toward nature. Group discussions and collaborative activities enhanced soft skills such as communication, teamwork, and leadership. The tranquil surroundings of the park offered a refreshing break from classroom routines, sparking curiosity and deeper learning. Overall, the visit was both educational and inspiring, fostering a lasting interest in sustainability and reinforcing theoretical knowledge through direct, meaningful experience.</p>\r\n', '2025-07-10-24-Victoria Park Visit 7th_July.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-07-10 07:09:12', '2025-07-10 07:09:12', NULL, NULL),
(314, 1, '1', '6', '2025-07-09', '2025', 'Victoria Park Visit', '<p>The educational visit to Victoria Park, Bhavnagar, was organized to offer B.Tech Semester 1 students a practical, real-world understanding of key ecological and environmental concepts. Immersed in the park&rsquo;s rich biodiversity, students explored themes such as conservation, ecology, and sustainability beyond the confines of the classroom. Observing various plant and animal species in their natural habitat deepened their understanding of ecological balance and highlighted the importance of urban green spaces. The visit also aimed to cultivate environmental awareness and a sense of responsibility toward nature. Through group discussions and collaborative tasks, students developed essential soft skills including communication, teamwork, and leadership. The serene environment provided a refreshing change of pace, igniting curiosity and enhancing learning. Overall, the visit proved to be both educational and inspiring, reinforcing academic concepts through meaningful, hands-on experience.</p>\r\n', '2025-07-09-92-Victoria Park Visit 9th_July.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-07-09 15:35:34', '2025-07-09 15:35:34', NULL, NULL),
(315, 1, '1', '7', '2025-07-09', '2025', 'Victoria Park Visit', '<p>The educational visit to Victoria Park, Bhavnagar, was organized to offer B.Tech Semester 1 students a practical, real-world understanding of key ecological and environmental concepts. Immersed in the park&rsquo;s rich biodiversity, students explored themes such as conservation, ecology, and sustainability beyond the confines of the classroom. Observing various plant and animal species in their natural habitat deepened their understanding of ecological balance and highlighted the importance of urban green spaces. The visit also aimed to cultivate environmental awareness and a sense of responsibility toward nature. Through group discussions and collaborative tasks, students developed essential soft skills including communication, teamwork, and leadership. The serene environment provided a refreshing change of pace, igniting curiosity and enhancing learning. Overall, the visit proved to be both educational and inspiring, reinforcing academic concepts through meaningful, hands-on experience.</p>\r\n', '2025-07-09-66-Victoria Park Visit 9th_July.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-07-09 15:35:50', '2025-07-09 15:35:50', NULL, NULL),
(317, 1, '1', '6', '2025-07-11', '2025', 'Parle G Bhavnagar', '<p>The visit to <strong>Parle (G.P. Manglani Foods Pvt. Ltd.)</strong> offered <strong>B.Tech. Semester 1</strong>&nbsp;students a practical insight into the food manufacturing industry, specifically biscuit production. Students observed key processes such as mixing, baking, and packaging, while learning about hygiene standards, automation, and quality control. The visit helped bridge classroom learning with real-world applications, giving students a better understanding of industrial practices and encouraging interest in the field of food technology and manufacturing.</p>\r\n', '2025-07-14-15-Parle Visit Btech 1st 11th_July.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-07-14 10:49:00', '2025-07-14 10:49:00', NULL, NULL),
(318, 1, '1', '6', '2025-07-18', '2025', 'VSSE – ISRO AHMEDABAD', '<p>The visit to the <strong>Vikram Sarabhai Space Exhibition Center (VSSEC), Ahmedabad</strong> provided students with a fascinating insight into India&rsquo;s achievements in space technology. The exhibition featured interactive models, satellite replicas, and informative displays of major ISRO missions like Chandrayaan and Mangalyaan. Students watched a 3D video showcasing various space missions and global space collaborations, enhancing their understanding of satellite functions and space exploration. A highlight of the visit was the life-size satellite model, where a live explanation of each component helped students connect theoretical knowledge with real-world applications. The experience was educational and inspiring, sparking curiosity about space science and showcasing the vital role ISRO plays in national and global advancements.</p>\r\n', '2025-07-21-34-ISRO (VSSEC) B.tech 3rd Z.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-07-21 05:35:03', '2025-07-21 05:35:03', NULL, NULL),
(319, 1, '5', '23', '2025-07-22', '2025', 'Odoo India Pvt Ltd.', '<p>Odoo India Pvt. Ltd., based in Gandhinagar, is the Indian subsidiary of Odoo S.A., a global leader in open-source business management software. The company focuses on developing and enhancing Odoo&rsquo;s modular ERP solutions, which cover key business areas such as CRM, accounting, inventory, HR, and more. Odoo India plays a vital role in product development, customer support, and service delivery across Asia, helping businesses streamline operations through flexible and user-friendly tools.</p>\r\n', '2025-07-22-35-Odoo Pvt. Ltd. Diploma 5th (22-07).pdf', 1, 0, '2025-07-22 13:14:57', '2025-07-22 13:14:57', NULL, NULL),
(320, 1, '1', '4', '2025-08-06', '2025', 'QTONZ INFOSOFT PVT. LTD.', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\">Qtonz Infosoft Pvt. Ltd., established in 2013 and headquartered in Rajkot, Gujarat, is a dynamic IT company specializing in delivering innovative digital solutions. With over a decade of experience, Qtonz has evolved into a trusted partner for businesses worldwide, offering a comprehensive range of services including mobile and web application development, game development, CMS solutions, and e-commerce platforms.</p>\r\n', '2025-09-10-17-Qtonz_6-8-25_Industry Visit B.Tech CE.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-09-10 10:48:03', '2025-09-10 10:48:03', NULL, NULL),
(321, 1, '1', '4', '2025-07-08', '2025', 'SARVOTTAM DAIRY', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\">The industry visit to Sarvottam Dairy, located at Sihor in Bhavnagar, Gujarat, is designed to offer students a practical understanding of how a modern dairy cooperative functions. Sarvottam Dairy, officially known as the Shree Bhavnagar District Cooperative Milk Producers&rsquo; Union Ltd., collects milk from over 600 village societies and processes it into various products like pasteurized milk, butter, and buttermilk. The visit aims to connect academic concepts with real-world applications in dairy technology, cooperative management, and rural entrepreneurship. It also encourages students to explore opportunities in food processing, supply chain management, and sustainable agriculture.</p>\r\n', '2025-09-10-49-8-7-2025_Industry Visit_1st B.Tech. CSE_Odd 2025.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-09-10 11:10:27', '2025-09-10 11:10:27', NULL, NULL),
(322, 1, '5', '564', '2025-09-11', '2025', 'Industrial Visit to Adite Tech', '<p>The <strong>Industrial Visit</strong> to <em>Adite Technologies LLP, Bhavnagar</em> on <strong>11th September 2025</strong>, organized for the <strong>Diploma IT Premium Program &ndash; 1st Semester</strong>, offered students exclusive exposure to real-world IT practices and emerging technologies such as <strong>React, Flutter, Django, and Flask</strong>. Through expert sessions and live demonstrations, they gained practical insights, professional guidance, and industry awareness. This premium experience not only enhanced their technical knowledge but also inspired confidence, innovation, and career readiness, aligning with the program&rsquo;s vision of shaping <strong>future-ready IT professionals</strong>.</p>\r\n', '2025-09-12-43-industry visit Diploma (1st-premium) 11-09.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-09-12 10:51:36', '2025-09-12 10:51:36', NULL, NULL),
(323, 4, '1', '53', '2025-09-01', '2025', 'Project Udaan  Adani Mundra', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><strong>Project Udaan &nbsp;Adani Mundra</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><strong>Project Udaan:</strong><br />\r\nProject Udaan is an educational outreach initiative by the Adani Foundation, inspired by<br />\r\nGautam Adani&#39;s childhood experience seeing Kandla Port. It offers students&mdash;especially from<br />\r\ngovernment schools&mdash;direct exposure to Adani&rsquo;s large-scale industrial operations at Mundra.<br />\r\nThe goal is to ignite entrepreneurial aspirations while aligning with the UN&rsquo;s Sustainable<br />\r\nDevelopment Goal on Quality Education.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Objective of Visit</strong><br />\r\nThe primary objective of the Project Udaan visit to Mundra for college students is to provide them with<br />\r\nmeaningful exposure to large-scale industrial operations and real-world applications of their academic<br />\r\nlearning. By visiting key Adani Group facilities&mdash;such as the Mundra Port, Adani Power thermal plant,<br />\r\nAdani Wilmar manufacturing units, and renewable energy setups&mdash;students gain first hand insight into<br />\r\ndiverse sectors like logistics, power generation, FMCG production, and sustainability. Additionally, the<br />\r\nexposure fosters entrepreneurial thinking and inspires students to pursue ambitious goals by witnessing<br />\r\nthe scale and vision behind global enterprises. The visit emphasizes the importance of sustainability</p>\r\n\r\n<p>and corporate responsibility, helping students understand how modern industries are adopting eco-<br />\r\nfriendly technologies. Overall, Project Udaan serves as a motivational and educational platform that</p>\r\n\r\n<p>encourages holistic growth, critical thinking, and a deeper understanding of India&#39;s industrial landscape.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>&nbsp;Students witness automation, large-scale operations, safety protocols, and logistics first hand.</li>\r\n	<li>&nbsp;It sparks awareness about industrial processes, renewable energy, manufacturing, and port operations.</li>\r\n	<li>&nbsp;The immersive experience fosters motivation, aspirations, and a broader understanding of modern industry.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>About Visit</strong><br />\r\nThese visits bridge the gap between academic theory and practical application by showcasing<br />\r\nadvanced technologies, sustainable practices, and integrated logistics systems in action.<br />\r\nStudents gain valuable insights into how industries operate on a global scale and are inspired<br />\r\nto pursue ambitious careers in sectors like energy, manufacturing, logistics, and technology.<br />\r\nThe visit also emphasizes the importance of discipline, teamwork, and time management, while<br />\r\nfostering entrepreneurial thinking and awareness of environmental responsibility.<br />\r\nAccommodation during the visit is arranged at Shantivihar (Shanti Vihar) Guest House in<br />\r\nMundra, which offers a peaceful and well-maintained environment for students. The stay<br />\r\nincludes clean and comfortable rooms, a spacious dining area, and serene surroundings that<br />\r\ncontribute to a refreshing experience. The food served is typically simple, vegetarian, and<br />\r\nnutritious, often described as &quot;satvik,&quot; though preferences may vary among students. Most<br />\r\nparticipants appreciate the warm hospitality and efficient management at the guest house,<br />\r\nwhich ensures timely meals, organized schedules, and cultural or recreational activities to<br />\r\nenhance the stay. While a few students have noted occasional concerns about food quality or<br />\r\ncleanliness, the overall experience at Shantivihar is positive and supportive of the educational<br />\r\ngoals of Project Udaan.</p>\r\n', '2025-09-17-35-industrial visit Report.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-09-17 03:04:35', '2025-09-17 03:04:35', NULL, NULL),
(324, 4, '1', '54', '2025-09-01', '2025', 'Project Udaan  Adani Mundra (P', '<p><strong>Project Udaan:</strong><br />\r\nProject Udaan is an educational outreach initiative by the Adani Foundation, inspired by<br />\r\nGautam Adani&#39;s childhood experience seeing Kandla Port. It offers students&mdash;especially from<br />\r\ngovernment schools&mdash;direct exposure to Adani&rsquo;s large-scale industrial operations at Mundra.<br />\r\nThe goal is to ignite entrepreneurial aspirations while aligning with the UN&rsquo;s Sustainable<br />\r\nDevelopment Goal on Quality Education.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Objective of Visit</strong><br />\r\nThe primary objective of the Project Udaan visit to Mundra for college students is to provide them with<br />\r\nmeaningful exposure to large-scale industrial operations and real-world applications of their academic<br />\r\nlearning. By visiting key Adani Group facilities&mdash;such as the Mundra Port, Adani Power thermal plant,<br />\r\nAdani Wilmar manufacturing units, and renewable energy setups&mdash;students gain first hand insight into<br />\r\ndiverse sectors like logistics, power generation, FMCG production, and sustainability. Additionally, the<br />\r\nexposure fosters entrepreneurial thinking and inspires students to pursue ambitious goals by witnessing<br />\r\nthe scale and vision behind global enterprises. The visit emphasizes the importance of sustainability</p>\r\n\r\n<p>and corporate responsibility, helping students understand how modern industries are adopting eco-<br />\r\nfriendly technologies. Overall, Project Udaan serves as a motivational and educational platform that</p>\r\n\r\n<p>encourages holistic growth, critical thinking, and a deeper understanding of India&#39;s industrial landscape.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>&nbsp;Students witness automation, large-scale operations, safety protocols, and logistics first hand.</li>\r\n	<li>&nbsp;It sparks awareness about industrial processes, renewable energy, manufacturing, and port operations.</li>\r\n	<li>&nbsp;The immersive experience fosters motivation, aspirations, and a broader understanding of modern industry.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>About Visit</strong><br />\r\nThese visits bridge the gap between academic theory and practical application by showcasing<br />\r\nadvanced technologies, sustainable practices, and integrated logistics systems in action.<br />\r\nStudents gain valuable insights into how industries operate on a global scale and are inspired<br />\r\nto pursue ambitious careers in sectors like energy, manufacturing, logistics, and technology.<br />\r\nThe visit also emphasizes the importance of discipline, teamwork, and time management, while<br />\r\nfostering entrepreneurial thinking and awareness of environmental responsibility.<br />\r\nAccommodation during the visit is arranged at Shantivihar (Shanti Vihar) Guest House in<br />\r\nMundra, which offers a peaceful and well-maintained environment for students. The stay<br />\r\nincludes clean and comfortable rooms, a spacious dining area, and serene surroundings that<br />\r\ncontribute to a refreshing experience. The food served is typically simple, vegetarian, and<br />\r\nnutritious, often described as &quot;satvik,&quot; though preferences may vary among students. Most<br />\r\nparticipants appreciate the warm hospitality and efficient management at the guest house,<br />\r\nwhich ensures timely meals, organized schedules, and cultural or recreational activities to<br />\r\nenhance the stay. While a few students have noted occasional concerns about food quality or<br />\r\ncleanliness, the overall experience at Shantivihar is positive and supportive of the educational<br />\r\ngoals of Project Udaan.</p>\r\n', '2025-09-17-61-industrial visit Report.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-09-17 02:57:30', '2025-09-17 02:57:30', NULL, NULL),
(325, 4, '1', '55', '2025-09-01', '2025', 'Project Udaan Adani Mundra ', '<p><strong>Project Udaan Adani Mundra (Port)-Mundra</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Project Udaan:</strong><br />\r\nProject Udaan is an educational outreach initiative by the Adani Foundation, inspired by<br />\r\nGautam Adani&#39;s childhood experience seeing Kandla Port. It offers students&mdash;especially from<br />\r\ngovernment schools&mdash;direct exposure to Adani&rsquo;s large-scale industrial operations at Mundra.<br />\r\nThe goal is to ignite entrepreneurial aspirations while aligning with the UN&rsquo;s Sustainable<br />\r\nDevelopment Goal on Quality Education.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Objective of Visit</strong><br />\r\nThe primary objective of the Project Udaan visit to Mundra for college students is to provide them with<br />\r\nmeaningful exposure to large-scale industrial operations and real-world applications of their academic<br />\r\nlearning. By visiting key Adani Group facilities&mdash;such as the Mundra Port, Adani Power thermal plant,<br />\r\nAdani Wilmar manufacturing units, and renewable energy setups&mdash;students gain first hand insight into<br />\r\ndiverse sectors like logistics, power generation, FMCG production, and sustainability. Additionally, the<br />\r\nexposure fosters entrepreneurial thinking and inspires students to pursue ambitious goals by witnessing<br />\r\nthe scale and vision behind global enterprises. The visit emphasizes the importance of sustainability</p>\r\n\r\n<p>and corporate responsibility, helping students understand how modern industries are adopting eco-<br />\r\nfriendly technologies. Overall, Project Udaan serves as a motivational and educational platform that</p>\r\n\r\n<p>encourages holistic growth, critical thinking, and a deeper understanding of India&#39;s industrial landscape.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>&nbsp;Students witness automation, large-scale operations, safety protocols, and logistics first hand.</li>\r\n	<li>&nbsp;It sparks awareness about industrial processes, renewable energy, manufacturing, and port operations.</li>\r\n	<li>&nbsp;The immersive experience fosters motivation, aspirations, and a broader understanding of modern industry.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>About Visit</strong><br />\r\nThese visits bridge the gap between academic theory and practical application by showcasing<br />\r\nadvanced technologies, sustainable practices, and integrated logistics systems in action.<br />\r\nStudents gain valuable insights into how industries operate on a global scale and are inspired<br />\r\nto pursue ambitious careers in sectors like energy, manufacturing, logistics, and technology.<br />\r\nThe visit also emphasizes the importance of discipline, teamwork, and time management, while<br />\r\nfostering entrepreneurial thinking and awareness of environmental responsibility.<br />\r\nAccommodation during the visit is arranged at Shantivihar (Shanti Vihar) Guest House in<br />\r\nMundra, which offers a peaceful and well-maintained environment for students. The stay<br />\r\nincludes clean and comfortable rooms, a spacious dining area, and serene surroundings that<br />\r\ncontribute to a refreshing experience. The food served is typically simple, vegetarian, and<br />\r\nnutritious, often described as &quot;satvik,&quot; though preferences may vary among students. Most<br />\r\nparticipants appreciate the warm hospitality and efficient management at the guest house,<br />\r\nwhich ensures timely meals, organized schedules, and cultural or recreational activities to<br />\r\nenhance the stay. While a few students have noted occasional concerns about food quality or<br />\r\ncleanliness, the overall experience at Shantivihar is positive and supportive of the educational<br />\r\ngoals of Project Udaan.</p>\r\n', '2025-09-17-71-industrial visit Report.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-09-17 03:01:14', '2025-09-17 03:01:14', NULL, NULL),
(326, 4, '2', '56', '2025-09-01', '2025', 'Project Udaan Adani Mundra', '<p><strong>Project Udaan &nbsp;Adani Mundra</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Project Udaan:</strong><br />\r\nProject Udaan is an educational outreach initiative by the Adani Foundation, inspired by<br />\r\nGautam Adani&#39;s childhood experience seeing Kandla Port. It offers students&mdash;especially from<br />\r\ngovernment schools&mdash;direct exposure to Adani&rsquo;s large-scale industrial operations at Mundra.<br />\r\nThe goal is to ignite entrepreneurial aspirations while aligning with the UN&rsquo;s Sustainable<br />\r\nDevelopment Goal on Quality Education.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Objective of Visit</strong><br />\r\nThe primary objective of the Project Udaan visit to Mundra for college students is to provide them with<br />\r\nmeaningful exposure to large-scale industrial operations and real-world applications of their academic<br />\r\nlearning. By visiting key Adani Group facilities&mdash;such as the Mundra Port, Adani Power thermal plant,<br />\r\nAdani Wilmar manufacturing units, and renewable energy setups&mdash;students gain first hand insight into<br />\r\ndiverse sectors like logistics, power generation, FMCG production, and sustainability. Additionally, the<br />\r\nexposure fosters entrepreneurial thinking and inspires students to pursue ambitious goals by witnessing<br />\r\nthe scale and vision behind global enterprises. The visit emphasizes the importance of sustainability</p>\r\n\r\n<p>and corporate responsibility, helping students understand how modern industries are adopting eco-<br />\r\nfriendly technologies. Overall, Project Udaan serves as a motivational and educational platform that</p>\r\n\r\n<p>encourages holistic growth, critical thinking, and a deeper understanding of India&#39;s industrial landscape.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>&nbsp;Students witness automation, large-scale operations, safety protocols, and logistics first hand.</li>\r\n	<li>&nbsp;It sparks awareness about industrial processes, renewable energy, manufacturing, and port operations.</li>\r\n	<li>&nbsp;The immersive experience fosters motivation, aspirations, and a broader understanding of modern industry.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>About Visit</strong><br />\r\nThese visits bridge the gap between academic theory and practical application by showcasing<br />\r\nadvanced technologies, sustainable practices, and integrated logistics systems in action.<br />\r\nStudents gain valuable insights into how industries operate on a global scale and are inspired<br />\r\nto pursue ambitious careers in sectors like energy, manufacturing, logistics, and technology.<br />\r\nThe visit also emphasizes the importance of discipline, teamwork, and time management, while<br />\r\nfostering entrepreneurial thinking and awareness of environmental responsibility.<br />\r\nAccommodation during the visit is arranged at Shantivihar (Shanti Vihar) Guest House in<br />\r\nMundra, which offers a peaceful and well-maintained environment for students. The stay<br />\r\nincludes clean and comfortable rooms, a spacious dining area, and serene surroundings that<br />\r\ncontribute to a refreshing experience. The food served is typically simple, vegetarian, and<br />\r\nnutritious, often described as &quot;satvik,&quot; though preferences may vary among students. Most<br />\r\nparticipants appreciate the warm hospitality and efficient management at the guest house,<br />\r\nwhich ensures timely meals, organized schedules, and cultural or recreational activities to<br />\r\nenhance the stay. While a few students have noted occasional concerns about food quality or<br />\r\ncleanliness, the overall experience at Shantivihar is positive and supportive of the educational<br />\r\ngoals of Project Udaan.</p>\r\n', '2025-09-17-94-industrial visit Report.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-09-17 03:06:19', '2025-09-17 03:06:19', NULL, NULL),
(327, 4, '2', '57', '2025-09-01', '2025', 'Project Udaan  Adani Mundra', '<p><strong>Project Udaan &nbsp;Adani Mundra</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Project Udaan:</strong><br />\r\nProject Udaan is an educational outreach initiative by the Adani Foundation, inspired by<br />\r\nGautam Adani&#39;s childhood experience seeing Kandla Port. It offers students&mdash;especially from<br />\r\ngovernment schools&mdash;direct exposure to Adani&rsquo;s large-scale industrial operations at Mundra.<br />\r\nThe goal is to ignite entrepreneurial aspirations while aligning with the UN&rsquo;s Sustainable<br />\r\nDevelopment Goal on Quality Education.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Objective of Visit</strong><br />\r\nThe primary objective of the Project Udaan visit to Mundra for college students is to provide them with<br />\r\nmeaningful exposure to large-scale industrial operations and real-world applications of their academic<br />\r\nlearning. By visiting key Adani Group facilities&mdash;such as the Mundra Port, Adani Power thermal plant,<br />\r\nAdani Wilmar manufacturing units, and renewable energy setups&mdash;students gain first hand insight into<br />\r\ndiverse sectors like logistics, power generation, FMCG production, and sustainability. Additionally, the<br />\r\nexposure fosters entrepreneurial thinking and inspires students to pursue ambitious goals by witnessing<br />\r\nthe scale and vision behind global enterprises. The visit emphasizes the importance of sustainability</p>\r\n\r\n<p>and corporate responsibility, helping students understand how modern industries are adopting eco-<br />\r\nfriendly technologies. Overall, Project Udaan serves as a motivational and educational platform that</p>\r\n\r\n<p>encourages holistic growth, critical thinking, and a deeper understanding of India&#39;s industrial landscape.</p>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>&nbsp;Students witness automation, large-scale operations, safety protocols, and logistics first hand.</li>\r\n	<li>&nbsp;It sparks awareness about industrial processes, renewable energy, manufacturing, and port operations.</li>\r\n	<li>&nbsp;The immersive experience fosters motivation, aspirations, and a broader understanding of modern industry.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>About Visit</strong><br />\r\nThese visits bridge the gap between academic theory and practical application by showcasing<br />\r\nadvanced technologies, sustainable practices, and integrated logistics systems in action.<br />\r\nStudents gain valuable insights into how industries operate on a global scale and are inspired<br />\r\nto pursue ambitious careers in sectors like energy, manufacturing, logistics, and technology.<br />\r\nThe visit also emphasizes the importance of discipline, teamwork, and time management, while<br />\r\nfostering entrepreneurial thinking and awareness of environmental responsibility.<br />\r\nAccommodation during the visit is arranged at Shantivihar (Shanti Vihar) Guest House in<br />\r\nMundra, which offers a peaceful and well-maintained environment for students. The stay<br />\r\nincludes clean and comfortable rooms, a spacious dining area, and serene surroundings that<br />\r\ncontribute to a refreshing experience. The food served is typically simple, vegetarian, and<br />\r\nnutritious, often described as &quot;satvik,&quot; though preferences may vary among students. Most<br />\r\nparticipants appreciate the warm hospitality and efficient management at the guest house,<br />\r\nwhich ensures timely meals, organized schedules, and cultural or recreational activities to<br />\r\nenhance the stay. While a few students have noted occasional concerns about food quality or<br />\r\ncleanliness, the overall experience at Shantivihar is positive and supportive of the educational<br />\r\ngoals of Project Udaan.</p>\r\n', '2025-09-17-90-industrial visit Report.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-09-17 03:07:36', '2025-09-17 03:07:36', NULL, NULL),
(328, 1, '5', '23', '2025-09-18', '2025', 'Visit to ISRO Space Applicatio', '<p>On 18th September 2025, Diploma IT students visited the ISRO &ndash; Space Applications Centre (SAC), Ahmedabad, as part of their academic enrichment program. The visit offered valuable exposure to satellite communication, remote sensing, payload development, and the application of IT in space research and operations. Interactive sessions with eminent SAC scientists, coupled with demonstrations of advanced satellite models, deepened students&rsquo; technical understanding and inspired innovative thinking. This experience not only bridged the gap between classroom learning and real-world practices but also motivated students to explore future opportunities in space technology and allied fields.</p>\r\n', '2025-09-22-20-ISRO Space Applications Centre (SAC) Diploma (3rd-B&C) 18-09.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-09-22 04:46:40', '2025-09-22 04:46:40', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `tbl_industry_visit` (`id`, `faculty_id`, `level_id`, `program_id`, `date`, `visit_year`, `visit_name`, `visit_description`, `report`, `is_active`, `is_delete`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `created_by`, `updated_by`) VALUES
(329, 8, '1', '89', '2025-09-23', '2025', 'ODOO GANDHINAGAR', '<p>To understand the functioning of an IT company specializing in ERP and business management<br />\r\nsolutions, gain exposure to real-world software development, consulting, and implementation<br />\r\npractices, and learn how Odoo supports businesses through its open-source ERP platform. The visit<br />\r\naims to bridge academic learning with industry practices and provide students with insights into<br />\r\ncareer opportunities and emerging IT trends.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Odoo In Private Limited (Tiny ERP Pvt. Ltd.), located at Infocity, Gandhinagar, is a leading IT<br />\r\ncompany established in 2007. It provides ERP and business management solutions such as CRM,<br />\r\nAccounting, HR, E-commerce, and Inventory, with consulting and support services for businesses.<br />\r\nThe company has around 100 employees and is recognized for its open-source ERP platform. Odoo<br />\r\nGandhinagar also hosts major events like the Odoo Community Days India, making it an important<br />\r\nhub for ERP development and IT services in India.</p>\r\n', '2025-10-04-95-BCA SEM 5 (2).pdf', 1, 0, '2025-10-04 09:11:40', '2025-10-04 09:11:40', NULL, NULL),
(330, 8, '2', '90', '2025-09-23', '2025', 'Odoo Gandhinagar', '<p>Odoo In Private Limited (Tiny ERP Pvt. Ltd.), located at Infocity, Gandhinagar, is a leading IT<br />\r\ncompany established in 2007. It provides ERP and business management solutions such as CRM,<br />\r\nAccounting, HR, E-commerce, and Inventory, with consulting and support services for businesses.<br />\r\nThe company has around 100 employees and is recognized for its open-source ERP platform. Odoo<br />\r\nGandhinagar also hosts major events like the Odoo Community Days India, making it an important<br />\r\nhub for ERP development and IT services in India.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>To understand the functioning of an IT company specializing in ERP and business management<br />\r\nsolutions, gain exposure to real-world software development, consulting, and implementation<br />\r\npractices, and learn how Odoo supports businesses through its open-source ERP platform. The visit<br />\r\naims to bridge academic learning with industry practices and provide students with insights into<br />\r\ncareer opportunities and emerging IT trends.</p>\r\n', '2025-10-04-45-BCA SEM 5 (2).pdf', 1, 0, '2025-10-04 09:16:47', '2025-10-04 09:16:47', NULL, NULL),
(331, 8, '1', '89', '2025-09-25', '2025', 'BISAG Gandhinagar ', '<p>The Bhaskaracharya National Institute for Space Applications and Geoinformatics (BISAG-N),<br />\r\nlocated in Gandhinagar, is an autonomous institute under the Ministry of Electronics and Information<br />\r\nTechnology (MeitY). It provides geospatial, remote sensing, and satellite communication services for<br />\r\ngovernance, planning, and development. BISAG-N develops GIS solutions, supports tele-education<br />\r\nthrough channels like Vande Gujarat and SWAYAM Prabha, and applies technology in agriculture,<br />\r\nwater resource management, disaster management, and infrastructure planning. With strong<br />\r\ngovernment support and advanced facilities, it plays a key role in projects like the PM-GatiShakti<br />\r\nmission. While challenges remain in data updating and keeping pace with rapid technological<br />\r\nchanges, BISAG-N continues to strengthen Gujarat and India&rsquo;s digital governance, education, and<br />\r\nresource management.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The objective of the visit is to provide students with practical exposure to geospatial technologies,<br />\r\nremote sensing, GIS applications, and satellite-based communication systems. It aims to help them<br />\r\nunderstand how these technologies are applied in governance, agriculture, education, disaster<br />\r\nmanagement, and infrastructure planning. The visit will also create awareness about the role of<br />\r\nBISAG-N in national projects like PM-GatiShakti and inspire students to explore career and research<br />\r\nopportunities in space applications and geoinformatics.</p>\r\n', '2025-10-04-79-BCA-3_INDUSTRY_VISIT.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-10-04 09:21:37', '2025-10-04 09:21:37', NULL, NULL),
(332, 3, '1', '132', '2025-09-25', '2025', 'BISAG Gandhinagar', '<p>The Bhaskaracharya National Institute for Space Applications and Geoinformatics (BISAG-N),<br />\r\nlocated in Gandhinagar, is an autonomous institute under the Ministry of Electronics and Information<br />\r\nTechnology (MeitY). It provides geospatial, remote sensing, and satellite communication services for<br />\r\ngovernance, planning, and development. BISAG-N develops GIS solutions, supports tele-education<br />\r\nthrough channels like Vande Gujarat and SWAYAM Prabha, and applies technology in agriculture,<br />\r\nwater resource management, disaster management, and infrastructure planning. With strong<br />\r\ngovernment support and advanced facilities, it plays a key role in projects like the PM-GatiShakti<br />\r\nmission. While challenges remain in data updating and keeping pace with rapid technological<br />\r\nchanges, BISAG-N continues to strengthen Gujarat and India&rsquo;s digital governance, education, and<br />\r\nresource management.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>The objective of the visit is to provide students with practical exposure to geospatial technologies,<br />\r\nremote sensing, GIS applications, and satellite-based communication systems. It aims to help them<br />\r\nunderstand how these technologies are applied in governance, agriculture, education, disaster<br />\r\nmanagement, and infrastructure planning. The visit will also create awareness about the role of<br />\r\nBISAG-N in national projects like PM-GatiShakti and inspire students to explore career and research<br />\r\nopportunities in space applications and geoinformatics.</p>\r\n', '2025-10-04-32-BSCIT_3_INDUSTRY_VISIT.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-10-04 09:24:57', '2025-10-04 09:24:57', NULL, NULL),
(333, 1, '1', '6', '2025-10-14', '2025', 'Industry Visit to Qtonz Infoso', '<p>The students of <strong>B.Tech. Semester 5 &ndash; Information Technology Department</strong> from <strong>Gyanmanjari Innovative University, Bhavnagar</strong>, visited <strong>Qtonz Infosoft Pvt. Ltd., Rajkot</strong>, gaining valuable exposure to the real-world IT environment. The visit offered deep insights into software development, web design, and digital innovation, where professionals emphasized the importance of creativity, teamwork, and continuous learning. Students explored various departments, witnessed live workflows, and interacted with industry experts who shared knowledge on emerging technologies like AI, automation, and responsive design. The experience proved highly inspiring and educational, bridging the gap between academic learning and practical industry applications.</p>\r\n', '2025-10-14-61-Industry Visit B.Tech (5th-C) 14-10.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-10-14 16:13:55', '2025-10-14 16:13:55', NULL, NULL),
(334, 1, '5', '23', '2025-10-14', '2025', 'Field Visit to Floatbot.AI Ind', '<p>The students of <strong>Diploma 5th Semester &ndash; Class D (Genius)</strong> from the <strong>Department of Information Technology, Gyanmanjari Innovative University, Bhavnagar</strong>, visited <strong>Floatbot.AI India Pvt. Ltd., Bhavnagar</strong> on <strong>14th October 2025</strong> for an insightful field visit. The session introduced students to the world of <strong>Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, and conversational automation</strong>, where experts explained how AI chatbots and virtual assistants are designed using <strong>NLP, Python, TensorFlow, and Dialogflow</strong>. Students observed live demonstrations of AI-based chatbot development, exploring both the technical and design aspects of automation. The experience enriched their understanding of real-world AI applications, data security, and ethical practices while inspiring them to pursue innovation and hands-on learning in the field of emerging technologies.</p>\r\n', '2025-10-14-97-Field Visit Diploma (5th-D) 14-10.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-10-14 16:25:18', '2025-10-14 16:25:18', NULL, NULL),
(335, 1, '5', '24', '2025-02-23', '2025', 'INDUSTRIAL VISIT at ADANIGROUP', '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><u><em><strong>Industry Profile:</strong></em></u><br />\r\nMundra port is known for its customer centric approach by providing higher productivity,<br />\r\ninnovation logistics solutions, faster turnaround of vessels and faster evacuation of containers from<br />\r\nthe port through double stacked trains. 5 Natural gateway to cargo clusters in North &amp; North west<br />\r\nIndia offering undisputable logistics cost advantage to exporters &amp; importers. Flagship port with<br />\r\nefficient multi-modal transport connectivity for seamless movement of cargo. Four containerter<br />\r\nminals with a combined capacity of 7.5 million TEUs. State-of the-art port that can accommodate<br />\r\nleviathans of sea. More than 35 services operating from Mundra offering global coverage of trade<br />\r\nlanes. We saw vessel and trucks by the bus when we leave main port. Faculty co-ordinator explain<br />\r\nsome thigs wonderfully. We laughing together, also enjoy some jokes and games.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><br />\r\n<u><em><strong>Adani Wilmar</strong></em></u><br />\r\nAdani Wilmar Limited (AWL) is a joint venture incorporated in January 1999 between Adani<br />\r\nGroup Conglomerate, the leaders in International trading &amp; Private Infrastructure and Wilmar<br />\r\nInternational Ltd. - Singapore, Asia&#39;s leading Agri-business group.A manufacturer of<br />\r\nedibleoils,includingsoybean,cottonseed and groundnut,based in India and selling under the<br />\r\nFortune, Raag and Jubilee brands. A manufacturer of edible oils, including soybean,<br />\r\ncottonseed and groundnut, based in India and selling under the Fortune, Raag and Jubilee<br />\r\nbrands. Adani group gifted all student by mills.</p>\r\n', '2025-10-20-61-ADANI MUDRA (1).pdf', 1, 0, '2025-10-20 15:07:44', '2025-10-20 15:07:44', NULL, NULL),
(336, 1, '5', '213', '2025-02-23', '2025', 'INDUSTRIAL VISIT at ADANIGROUP', '<p><u><em><strong>Industry Profile:</strong></em></u><br />\r\nMundra port is known for its customer centric approach by providing higher productivity,<br />\r\ninnovation logistics solutions, faster turnaround of vessels and faster evacuation of containers from<br />\r\nthe port through double stacked trains. 5 Natural gateway to cargo clusters in North &amp; North west<br />\r\nIndia offering undisputable logistics cost advantage to exporters &amp; importers. Flagship port with<br />\r\nefficient multi-modal transport connectivity for seamless movement of cargo. Four containerter<br />\r\nminals with a combined capacity of 7.5 million TEUs. State-of the-art port that can accommodate<br />\r\nleviathans of sea. More than 35 services operating from Mundra offering global coverage of trade<br />\r\nlanes. We saw vessel and trucks by the bus when we leave main port. Faculty co-ordinator explain<br />\r\nsome thigs wonderfully. We laughing together, also enjoy some jokes and games.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><br />\r\n<em><u><strong>Adani Wilmar</strong></u></em><br />\r\nAdani Wilmar Limited (AWL) is a joint venture incorporated in January 1999 between Adani<br />\r\nGroup Conglomerate, the leaders in International trading &amp; Private Infrastructure and Wilmar<br />\r\nInternational Ltd. - Singapore, Asia&#39;s leading Agri-business group.A manufacturer of<br />\r\nedibleoils,includingsoybean,cottonseed and groundnut,based in India and selling under the<br />\r\nFortune, Raag and Jubilee brands. A manufacturer of edible oils, including soybean,<br />\r\ncottonseed and groundnut, based in India and selling under the Fortune, Raag and Jubilee<br />\r\nbrands. Adani group gifted all student by mills.</p>\r\n', '2025-10-20-27-ADANI MUDRA (1).pdf', 1, 0, '2025-10-20 15:13:20', '2025-10-20 15:13:20', NULL, NULL),
(337, 1, '1', '3', '2025-02-23', '2025', 'INDUSTRIAL VISIT at ADANIGROUP', '<p><u><em><strong>Industry Profile:</strong></em></u><br />\r\nMundra port is known for its customer centric approach by providing higher productivity,<br />\r\ninnovation logistics solutions, faster turnaround of vessels and faster evacuation of containers from<br />\r\nthe port through double stacked trains. 5 Natural gateway to cargo clusters in North &amp; North west<br />\r\nIndia offering undisputable logistics cost advantage to exporters &amp; importers. Flagship port with<br />\r\nefficient multi-modal transport connectivity for seamless movement of cargo. Four containerter<br />\r\nminals with a combined capacity of 7.5 million TEUs. State-of the-art port that can accommodate<br />\r\nleviathans of sea. More than 35 services operating from Mundra offering global coverage of trade<br />\r\nlanes. We saw vessel and trucks by the bus when we leave main port. Faculty co-ordinator explain<br />\r\nsome thigs wonderfully. We laughing together, also enjoy some jokes and games.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><br />\r\n<u><em><strong>Adani Wilmar</strong></em></u><br />\r\nAdani Wilmar Limited (AWL) is a joint venture incorporated in January 1999 between Adani<br />\r\nGroup Conglomerate, the leaders in International trading &amp; Private Infrastructure and Wilmar<br />\r\nInternational Ltd. - Singapore, Asia&#39;s leading Agri-business group.A manufacturer of<br />\r\nedibleoils,includingsoybean,cottonseed and groundnut,based in India and selling under the<br />\r\nFortune, Raag and Jubilee brands. A manufacturer of edible oils, including soybean,<br />\r\ncottonseed and groundnut, based in India and selling under the Fortune, Raag and Jubilee<br />\r\nbrands. Adani group gifted all student by mills.</p>\r\n', '2025-10-20-54-ADANI MUDRA (1).pdf', 1, 0, '2025-10-20 15:19:51', '2025-10-20 15:19:51', NULL, NULL),
(338, 1, '1', '212', '2025-02-23', '2025', 'INDUSTRIAL VISIT at ADANIGROUP', '<p><u><em><strong>Industry Profile:</strong></em></u><br />\r\nMundra port is known for its customer centric approach by providing higher productivity,<br />\r\ninnovation logistics solutions, faster turnaround of vessels and faster evacuation of containers from<br />\r\nthe port through double stacked trains. 5 Natural gateway to cargo clusters in North &amp; North west<br />\r\nIndia offering undisputable logistics cost advantage to exporters &amp; importers. Flagship port with<br />\r\nefficient multi-modal transport connectivity for seamless movement of cargo. Four containerter<br />\r\nminals with a combined capacity of 7.5 million TEUs. State-of the-art port that can accommodate<br />\r\nleviathans of sea. More than 35 services operating from Mundra offering global coverage of trade<br />\r\nlanes. We saw vessel and trucks by the bus when we leave main port. Faculty co-ordinator explain<br />\r\nsome thigs wonderfully. We laughing together, also enjoy some jokes and games.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><br />\r\n<u><em><strong>Adani Wilmar</strong></em></u><br />\r\nAdani Wilmar Limited (AWL) is a joint venture incorporated in January 1999 between Adani<br />\r\nGroup Conglomerate, the leaders in International trading &amp; Private Infrastructure and Wilmar<br />\r\nInternational Ltd. - Singapore, Asia&#39;s leading Agri-business group.A manufacturer of<br />\r\nedibleoils,includingsoybean,cottonseed and groundnut,based in India and selling under the<br />\r\nFortune, Raag and Jubilee brands. A manufacturer of edible oils, including soybean,<br />\r\ncottonseed and groundnut, based in India and selling under the Fortune, Raag and Jubilee<br />\r\nbrands. Adani group gifted all student by mills.</p>\r\n', '2025-10-20-83-ADANI MUDRA (1).pdf', 1, 0, '2025-10-20 15:21:19', '2025-10-20 15:21:19', NULL, NULL),
(339, 1, '1', '3', '2025-07-29', '2025', 'Thermal Power Station Padva', '<p style=\"margin-left:97px\"><span style=\"font-size:15.960000038146973pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Times New Roman\',serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><strong>Objective&nbsp;&nbsp;</strong></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:96px; margin-right:76px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Times New Roman\',serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The primary objective of the industrial visit was to provide students with practical exposure to&nbsp; the real-time functioning of a thermal power plant. By visiting the Bhavnagar Thermal Power&nbsp; Station, students gained a deeper understanding of how electricity is generated using thermal&nbsp; energy, how various components like boilers, turbines, and control systems operate, and how&nbsp; power is managed and transmitted efficiently. The visit aimed to bridge the gap between&nbsp; theoretical classroom learning and actual industrial practices, thereby enhancing students&#39;&nbsp; technical knowledge, observational skills, and interest in power system engineering..&nbsp;</span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:96px\"><span style=\"font-size:15.960000038146973pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Times New Roman\',serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><strong>About Activities:&nbsp;</strong></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:96px; margin-right:89px\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Times New Roman\',serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">During the visit, students were guided through various sections of the power plant including: </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:9.960000038146973pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Noto Sans Symbols\',sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">&bull; </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Times New Roman\',serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><strong>Boiler Unit </strong></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Times New Roman\',serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">&ndash; Introduction to steam generation and combustion process.&nbsp;</span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:121px; margin-right:77px\"><span style=\"font-size:9.960000038146973pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Noto Sans Symbols\',sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">&bull; </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Times New Roman\',serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><strong>Turbine Section </strong></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Times New Roman\',serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">&ndash; Demonstration of energy conversion from thermal to mechanical&nbsp; and then to electrical.&nbsp;</span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:121px; margin-right:77px\"><span style=\"font-size:9.960000038146973pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Noto Sans Symbols\',sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">&bull; </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Times New Roman\',serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><strong>Control Room </strong></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Times New Roman\',serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">&ndash; Understanding centralized control and monitoring of power plant&nbsp; operations.&nbsp;</span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:121px; margin-right:76px\"><span style=\"font-size:9.960000038146973pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Noto Sans Symbols\',sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">&bull; </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Times New Roman\',serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><strong>Cooling System &amp; Ash Handling </strong></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Times New Roman\',serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">&ndash; Insight into thermal efficiency and waste&nbsp; management.&nbsp;</span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:96px; margin-right:76px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Times New Roman\',serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">Engineers and staff at the station explained each process in detail, and interactive sessions were&nbsp; held to clarify student doubts.The visit was successfully accomplished under the valuable&nbsp; guidance and coordination of </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Times New Roman\',serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><strong>Prof. Jaydipsinh Parmar</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Times New Roman\',serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">, </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Times New Roman\',serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><strong>Prof. Disha Siddhapura</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Times New Roman\',serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">, and </span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Times New Roman\',serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><strong>Prof.&nbsp; Pankaj Chaudhary</strong></span></span></span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Times New Roman\',serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">, whose efforts ensured a well-organized and educational experience for&nbsp; all the participating students.&nbsp;</span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:97px\"><span style=\"font-size:15.960000038146973pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Times New Roman\',serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><strong>Conclusion&nbsp;</strong></span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"margin-left:96px; margin-right:76px; text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><span style=\"font-family:\'Times New Roman\',serif\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">The industrial visit to the GNITE Thermal Power Station was highly beneficial.&nbsp; It provided students with valuable insights into large-scale power production and helped them&nbsp; relate their theoretical knowledge to practical applications. The coordination and support of the&nbsp; faculty members made the visit informative and well-Organized</span></span></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n', '2025-10-31-18-2. Industry Visit Thermal Power plant visit DE3_EC.pdf', 1, 0, '2025-10-31 02:31:33', '2025-10-31 02:31:33', NULL, NULL),
