(15, 'demo', 'demo', '', '2024-09-06-52-logo.jpg', '', '2024-09-01', 0, 1, '2024-09-06 07:59:49', '2024-09-06 07:59:49', NULL, NULL),
(16, 'A grand Triranga yatra was organized by the Divya Bhaskar group on the occasion of 15th August in Bhavnagar. The purpose of which was to unite all the people and celebrate Independence Day together. In which the students of Gyanmanjari Innovative University participated in this grand rally as part of Tricolor Yatra.Participants:Students of various departments and NSS volunteers participated in this rally. Everyone enthusiastically participated in this rally and joined this grand Triranga rally.Event Details Date: [15 August 2024] Venue: Water Tank, Bhavnagar Time: 10 AM To 12 PM', 'Triranga Yatra Report', '', '2024-09-14-82-5. Tiranga Yatra_report.pdf', '', '2024-08-15', 1, 0, '2024-09-14 04:23:22', '2024-09-14 04:23:22', NULL, NULL),
(17, 'To honor and appreciate the Dream Of Mahatma Gandhi to make a Clean India and to guide and shape the minds of Students to make a clean and Green Environment around us.\r\norganized by: Gyanmanjari Institute of Arts. and NSS Unit', 'Swachhata Shreni Drive- 4 with “Swachhata Hi Sava” theme.', '', '2024-10-15-86-Gyanmanjari Innovative University- Bhavnagar and GMIT.pdf', '', '2024-10-04', 1, 0, '2024-10-15 03:46:42', '2024-10-15 03:46:42', NULL, NULL),
(18, 'Gyanmanjari Innovative University, driven by its commitment to environmental responsibility, has actively embraced the Vibrant Gujarat 2024-5 P Campaign to promote environmental awareness among its students. Aligned with the guidelines from the Gujarat Energy Development Agency (GEDA), the college initiated a pledge taking ceremony on 09/01/2024 to engage students in the mission of sustainable living.', 'VIBRANT GUJARAT PLEGDE 2024: ENVIRONMENTAL AWARENESS CAMPAIGN On 09thJanuary,2024', '', '2024-10-19-10-VIBRANT GUJARAT ENVIRONMENTAL AWARENESS CAMPAIGN.pdf', '', '2024-01-09', 1, 0, '2024-10-19 06:42:09', '2024-10-19 06:42:09', NULL, NULL),
(19, 'During the event, Prime Minister Shri Narendra Modi emphasized the concept of a developed India by 2047. His address from the ramparts of the Red Fort resonated with the dreams and aspirations of 1.4 billion citizens. To achieve this vision, hard work is essential, but equally crucial is our national character. Nations that have  progressed and overcome challenges share a common catalyst: their strong national character. Strengthening our national character is paramount as we move forward. The purpose of the “Viksit Bharat @2047: Voice of Youth” meeting was to engage young minds in discussions and inspire them to contribute actively towards building a developed India by the year 2047. The event aimed to foster a sense of national character, unity, and excellence in production. Prime Minister Shri Narendra Modi emphasized the importance of these aspects during his address,\r\nencouraging participants to work diligently and uphold the vision of progress for our nation. The event served as a platform for dialogue, awareness, and collective resolve toward achieving a brighter future for India.The meeting aimed to ignite enthusiasm and commitment among the youth, aligning their efforts with the vision of a developed India.\r\nApproximately 80 volunteers attended this Meeting.', 'VIKSIT BHARAT @2047: Voice of Youth Meeting On 11th December 2023', '', '2024-10-19-79-VIKSIT BHARAT @2047 Meeting.pdf', '', '2023-12-11', 1, 0, '2024-10-19 06:48:42', '2024-10-19 06:48:42', NULL, NULL),
(20, 'Gyanmanjari Innovative University organized a workshop guider by Young Indians and EMRI (Emergency Management and Research Institute) regarding accidental first response and CPR training. These programs play a crucial role in equipping individuals with life-saving skills.\r\nCPR Training:\r\n•	Cardiopulmonary resuscitation (CPR) is a vital skill that can save lives during cardiac emergencies.\r\n•	CPR involves chest compressions and rescue breaths to maintain\r\nblood circulation and oxygen supply.\r\n•	Training covers techniques such as:\r\no	Hands-only CPR: Focusing on chest compressions without mouth-to-mouth breathing.\r\no	Full CPR: Combining chest compressions with rescue breaths.\r\nApprox 85 Participants learnt how to recognize signs of cardiac arrest, perform CPR correctly.\r\n', 'Accidental First Response and CPR Training by YI and EMRI On 06th February,2024', '', '2024-10-19-92-cpr training by yi and emri.pdf', '', '2024-02-06', 1, 0, '2024-10-19 06:58:28', '2024-10-19 06:58:28', NULL, NULL),
(21, 'Joy of Giving is an activity that is organized to give joy to other people. Every year, Joy of Giving activity is organized at Gyanmanjari Innovative University, this activity is an activity of collecting clothes and donating them to the needy people. Every month, a social activity is organized at Gyanmanjari Innovative University, which can be useful in the society in some way. One of the important activities of Joy of Giving is the Cloth Donation Mega Drive.\r\nIn this clothes donation mega drive, 08 coordinators including Principal of Pharmacy college Dr. Viram J. Parmar who is the Director of NSS and Social Activities, joined this drive and around more than 60 students and NSS volunteers participated. Everyone participated enthusiastically in this clothes donation drive. \r\nThe \"Joy of Giving\" Cloth Donation Drive is an annual initiative aimed at spreading warmth, kindness, and hope to those in need. The primary purpose of this drive is to collect gently used and new clothes and distribute them to underprivileged individuals, including the homeless, orphaned children, and families in need. Through this initiative, we aim to Support the Needy: Provide clothing to those who lack basic necessities, ensuring they stay warm and dignified, Promote Sustainable Giving: Encourage the community to donate reusable clothes instead of discarding them, reducing waste, Inspire Social Responsibility: Foster a culture of compassion and generosity among individuals and organizations and bring Smiles & Comfort: Spread happiness by ensuring that no one has to suffer due to a lack of adequate clothing. By organizing the \"Joy of Giving\" drive every year, we create a meaningful impact on countless lives and strengthen the spirit of giving in our community.\r\nJoy of Giving is an activity of giving joy. Through the Joy of Giving activity, student volunteers collected clothes from various circles of Bhavnagar from 24th January to 26th January 2025, in which many clothes were donated by people who had the spirit of donation. Later, those clothes were separated according to size and distributed on 1st February 2025 in Kumbharwada, Tilaknagar and Juna Bandar of Bhavnagar.', 'Joy Of Giving 2025', '', '2025-02-07-73-joy of giving report 2025.pdf', '', '2025-01-24', 1, 0, '2025-02-07 09:28:33', '2025-02-07 09:28:33', NULL, NULL),
(22, 'At Gyanmanjari Innovative University, we aim to foster holistic development through the integration of physical, mental, and spiritual well-being. As part of our ongoing commitment to social responsibility and active NSS participation, “International Yoga Day” is celebrated as a significant event in our annual calendar of activities. \r\nGyanmanjari Innovative University successfully celebrated International Yoga Day on 21st June 2025 with great enthusiasm. The event aimed to promote physical, mental, and spiritual well-being through the practice of yoga, as part of the university’s commitment to NSS and social responsibility.', 'International Yoga Day 2025', '', '2025-07-02-89-International Yog Day Report 2025.pdf', '', '2025-06-21', 1, 0, '2025-07-02 03:36:08', '2025-07-02 03:36:08', NULL, NULL),
(23, 'An initiative of Swachhata Abhiyan has been carried out by Gyanmanjari Innovative University, in which on 20 th February by commerce department organized a cleaning campaign on the theme of world of social justice.\r\nParticipants:\r\nIn this cleaning drive, 6 staff members including the commerce Head of Department commerce and teachers joined this drive and around 60 students and NSS volunteers participated. Everyone enthusiastically participated in this cleanliness campaign and joined this cleaning campaign.\r\nEvent Details\r\nDate: 20th February, 2025\r\n\r\nVenue: Bor talav lack Bhavnagar \r\nTime: 9:30am to 12:00 pm\r\n\r\nPurpose of Event \r\n1.	Environmental Awareness: Promotes a culture of cleanliness and environmental stewardship among students and staff. \r\n2.	Community Engagement: Encourages participation and teamwork, fostering a sense of community and responsibility. \r\n3.	Health Benefits: Reduces litter and waste, contributing to a healthier campus environment. \r\n4.	Sustainability Education: Provides an opportunity to educate participants on sustainability practices and waste management. \r\n5.	Leadership Development: Empowers students to take initiative and lead community service efforts. \r\n6.	Campus Pride: Enhances the aesthetic appeal of the university, instilling pride among students and faculty. \r\nThis monthly program not only aims to keep the campus clean but also strives to instill lifelong habits of cleanliness and environmental care in participants.\r\nConclusion\r\n\r\nCleanliness campaign which was done by commerce Department. The Head commerce of and Faculty and students of commerce participated in this campaign. Which was successfully completed.\r\n', 'Swachchhta Abhiyan and  world Day of social justice Report 2025', '', '2025-07-02-24-Swachchhta Abhiyan & World Day of Social Justice Report 2025.pdf', '', '2025-02-20', 1, 0, '2025-07-02 04:02:47', '2025-07-02 04:02:47', NULL, NULL),
(24, 'On 23rd May, 2025 at GMIU campus (Computer Lab – FF25), Gyanmanjari Innovative University (GMIU) in collaboration with the Faith Foundation (Baroda) jointly organized a Tobacco Awareness Activity on 23rd May 2025 to spread awareness about the serious health hazards of tobacco use. The event was conducted at Computer Lab – FF25 and was a meaningful step toward building a tobacco-free mindset among the youth and academic community.\r\nThe activity was coordinated by Prof. Pradip Prajapati, who ensured smooth execution of the entire event. The event was also graced by the presence of Dr. Viram Parmar Sir, Director of NSS and Social Activities, who inspired students to become health ambassadors and agents of change in society.\r\nAlthough Dr. H.M. Nimbark, Provost and CEO of GMIU, was not present at the event, his continuous support and encouragement played a key role in making this initiative possible. His commitment to student development and health-related awareness activities has always been a guiding force behind such meaningful programs.\r\nAs a mark of appreciation, the university welcomed the Faith Foundation team with a token gift.\r\nFaith Foundation is a reputed NGO based in Vadodara, Gujarat, founded by Suzaane Christian in 2005. The organization is dedicated to promoting a healthy lifestyle free from addiction, especially focusing on de-addiction, tobacco control, HIV/AIDS support, education, and women\'s empowerment. The foundation is well-known for its impactful programs like the Yellow Line Campaign and anti-tobacco rallies, working actively with communities and institutions to build awareness and inspire behavior change. GMIU is proud to be one of its collaborative partners.', 'NO Tobacco Day celebration activity report 23rd May, 2025', '', '2025-07-02-46-NO Tobacco Day celebration activity report 23rd May, 2025.pdf', '', '2025-05-23', 1, 0, '2025-07-02 04:16:11', '2025-07-02 04:16:11', NULL, NULL),
(25, 'Gyanmanjari Innovative University celebrated Van Mahotsav on 4th September 2025, in collaboration with the Forest Department. The event was organized to promote environmental awareness and the importance of tree plantation for a greener and healthier future.', 'Van Mahotsav Report', '', '2025-09-24-35-Screenshot (235).png', '', '2025-09-04', 1, 0, '2025-09-24 10:07:36', '2025-09-24 10:07:36', NULL, NULL),
(26, 'Gyanmanjari Innovative University celebrated Van Mahotsav on 4th September 2025, in collaboration with the Forest Department. The event was organized to promote environmental awareness and the importance of tree plantation for a greener and healthier future.', 'Van Mahotsav Report', '', '2025-09-24-69-Van Mahotsa Report.pdf', '', '2025-09-04', 1, 0, '2025-09-24 10:11:53', '2025-09-24 10:11:53', NULL, NULL),
(27, 'Our NSS volunteers from Gyanmanjari Innovative University actively participated in the Samudra Se Samrudhi program, a visionary initiative inaugurated by the Hon’ble Prime Minister of India, Shri Narendra Modi. The program emphasizes the importance of sustainable development, marine resources, and community engagement. The event was organized at Jawahar Maidan, Bhavnagar, where our NSS volunteers contributed through their enthusiastic involvement, showcasing commitment towards national initiatives and environmental responsibility.', 'Samudra se Samrudhi Report - 2025', '', '2025-09-30-10-Samudra Se Samrudhi Event Report.pdf', '', '2025-09-20', 1, 0, '2025-09-30 05:12:11', '2025-09-30 05:12:11', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `tbl_nss_about` (`id`, `description`, `is_active`, `is_delete`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `created_by`, `updated_by`) VALUES
(1, '<p>About NSS test</p>\r\n', 0, 1, '2024-01-08 10:10:38', '2024-01-08 10:10:38', NULL, NULL),
(2, '<p>About NSS</p>\r\n', 0, 1, '2024-01-08 10:16:27', '2024-01-08 10:16:27', NULL, NULL),
(3, '<p><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif\">The National Service Scheme (NSS) is an Indian government-sponsored public service program conducted by the Department of Youth Affairs and Sports of the Government of India. Popularly known as NSS, the scheme was launched in Gandhiji&rsquo;s Centenary year, 1969.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif\">Aimed at developing student&rsquo;s personality through community service, NSS is a voluntary association of young people in Colleges, Universities and at +2 level working for a campus-community linkage.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif\">The cardinal principle of the NSS programme is that it is organised by the students themselves, and both students and teachers through their combined participation in community service, get a sense of involvement in the tasks of nation building.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif\">After independence the University Grants Commission, headed by S. Radhakrishnan, recommended the introduction of voluntary national service in academic institutions.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman,Times,serif\">In May 1969, a conference of student representatives (of universities and institutions of higher education) convened by the Ministry of Education and the University Grants Commission also unanimously agreed that a national-service scheme could be an instrument for national integration. The details were soon worked out and the Planning Commission sanctioned an outlay of Rs. five crores for the NSS during the Fourth Five-Year Plan, stipulating that the NSS be a pilot project in select institutions and universities. On 24 September 1969, then-Union Education Minister V.K.R.V. Rao launched the NSS at 37 universities in all states. The scheme has been extended to all states and universities in the country, and also +2-level institutes in many states.</span></p>\r\n', 0, 1, '2024-01-09 10:13:52', '2024-01-09 10:13:52', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `tbl_nss_about` (`id`, `description`, `is_active`, `is_delete`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `created_by`, `updated_by`) VALUES
(4, '<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><strong>NSS History</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\">The National Service Scheme (NSS) is an Indian government-sponsored public service program conducted by the Department of Youth Affairs and Sports of the Government of India. Popularly known as NSS, the scheme was launched in Gandhiji&rsquo;s Centenary year, 1969.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\">Aimed at developing student&rsquo;s personality through community service, NSS is a voluntary association of young people in Colleges, Universities and at +2 level working for a campus-community linkage.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\">The cardinal principle of the NSS programme is that it is organised by the students themselves, and both students and teachers through their combined participation in community service, get a sense of involvement in the tasks of nation building.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\">After independence the University Grants Commission, headed by S. Radhakrishnan, recommended the introduction of voluntary national service in academic institutions.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\">In May 1969, a conference of student representatives (of universities and institutions of higher education) convened by the Ministry of Education and the University Grants Commission also unanimously agreed that a national-service scheme could be an instrument for national integration. The details were soon worked out and the Planning Commission sanctioned an outlay of Rs. five crores for the NSS during the Fourth Five-Year Plan, stipulating that the NSS be a pilot project in select institutions and universities. On 24 September 1969, then-Union Education Minister V.K.R.V. Rao launched the NSS at 37 universities in all states. The scheme has been extended to all states and universities in the country, and also +2-level institutes in many states.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><strong>Motto of NSS</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\">&ldquo;NOT ME, BUT YOU&rdquo; This reflects the essence of democratic living and upholds the need for selfless service and appreciation of the other person&rsquo;s point of view and also to show consideration for fellow human beings. It underlines that the welfare of an individual is ultimately dependent on the welfare of society on the whole.</p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><strong>Symbol of NSS</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><img src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,', 0, 1, '2024-02-09 09:46:39', '2024-02-09 09:46:39', NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `tbl_nss_about` (`id`, `description`, `is_active`, `is_delete`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `created_by`, `updated_by`) VALUES
(5, '<h3><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><span style=\"color:#ba2a21\"><strong>NSS History</strong></span></span></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color:#000000\">The National Service Scheme (NSS) is an Indian government-sponsored public service program conducted by the Department of Youth Affairs and Sports of the Government of India. Popularly known as NSS, the scheme was launched in Gandhiji&rsquo;s Centenary year, 1969.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color:#000000\">Aimed at developing student&rsquo;s personality through community service, NSS is a voluntary association of young people in Colleges, Universities and at +2 level working for a campus-community linkage.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color:#000000\">The cardinal principle of the NSS programme is that it is organised by the students themselves, and both students and teachers through their combined participation in community service, get a sense of involvement in the tasks of nation building.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color:#000000\">After independence the University Grants Commission, headed by S. Radhakrishnan, recommended the introduction of voluntary national service in academic institutions.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color:#000000\">In May 1969, a conference of student representatives (of universities and institutions of higher education) convened by the Ministry of Education and the University Grants Commission also unanimously agreed that a national-service scheme could be an instrument for national integration. The details were soon worked out and the Planning Commission sanctioned an outlay of Rs. five crores for the NSS during the Fourth Five-Year Plan, stipulating that the NSS be a pilot project in select institutions and universities. On 24 September 1969, then-Union Education Minister V.K.R.V. Rao launched the NSS at 37 universities in all states. The scheme has been extended to all states and universities in the country, and also +2-level institutes in many states.</span></p>\r\n', 1, 0, '2024-02-09 16:09:57', '2024-02-09 16:09:57', NULL, NULL),
(6, '<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><span style=\"color:#ba2a21\"><strong>Motto of NSS</strong></span></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color:#000000\">&ldquo;NOT ME, BUT YOU&rdquo; This reflects the essence of democratic living and upholds the need for selfless service and appreciation of the other person&rsquo;s point of view and also to show consideration for fellow human beings. It underlines that the welfare of an individual is ultimately dependent on the welfare of society on the whole.</span></p>\r\n', 1, 0, '2024-02-09 16:11:54', '2024-02-09 16:11:54', NULL, NULL),
(7, '<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><span style=\"color:#ba2a21\"><strong>Symbole of NSS</strong></span></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><img alt=\"File:NSS-symbol.jpeg - Wikipedia\" src=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/90/NSS-symbol.jpeg\" style=\"height:180px; width:180px\" /></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color:#000000\">The symbol for the NSS has been based on the giant Rath Wheel of the world famous Konark Sun Temple (The Black Pagoda) situated in Orissa, India. The wheel portrays the cycle of creation, preservation and release and signifies the movement in life across time and space, the symbol thus stands for continuity as well as change and implies the continuous striving of NSS for social change. The eight bars in the wheel represent the 24 hours of a day. The red colour indicates that the volunteer is full of young blood that is lively, active, energetic and full of high spirit. The navy blue colour indicates the cosmos of which the NSS is tiny part, ready to contribute its share for the welfare of the mankind.</span></p>\r\n', 1, 0, '2024-02-09 16:18:31', '2024-02-09 16:18:31', NULL, NULL),
(8, '<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><span style=\"color:#ba2a21\"><strong>Aim of NSS&nbsp;</strong></span></h3>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color:#000000\">The programme aims to inculcate social welfare in students, and to provide service to society without bias. NSS volunteers work to ensure that everyone who is needy gets help to enhance their standard of living and lead a life of dignity. In doing so, volunteers learn from people in villages how to lead a good life despite a scarcity of resources. it also provides help in natural and man-made disasters by providing food, clothing and first aid to the disaster victims.</span></p>\r\n', 1, 0, '2024-02-09 16:22:25', '2024-02-09 16:22:25', NULL, NULL),
(9, '<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<h3><span style=\"color:#ba2a21\"><strong>Objectives of NSS&nbsp;</strong></span></h3>\r\n\r\n<ul>\r\n	<li>understand themselves in relation to their community;</li>\r\n	<li>identify the needs and problems of the community and involve them in problem&nbsp; solving process;</li>\r\n	<li>develop among themselves a sense of social and civic responsibility;</li>\r\n	<li>utilize their knowledge in finding practical solution to individual and community problems;</li>\r\n	<li>develop competence required for group living and sharing of responsibilities;</li>\r\n	<li>gain skills in mobilizing community participation;</li>\r\n	<li>acquire leadership qualities and democratic attitude;</li>\r\n	<li>develop capacity to meet emergencies and natural disasters</li>\r\n	<li>practice national integration and social harmon</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><strong>Sports, Social and Cultural Activities are run at Gyanmanjari Innovative University</strong></span></span></p>\r\n', 1, 0, '2024-02-09 16:24:16', '2024-02-09 16:24:16', NULL, NULL);
